  "_comment": "Per-card outcome assertions, read by tests/cards/test_every_card_works.py and tests/cards/test_hand_written_cards.py. The sandbox is described in the former: player 0 starts at 40 life with 30 lands and 2 other permanents, an empty hand once the card under test is played, and player 1 at 40 life. Every hand-written card must appear here -- gate 5 refuses a card nobody has asserted anything about -- but a zone-only entry is the floor, not coverage: it says the card resolved to the right place and nothing about what it did. `python scripts/audit_cards.py` still reports those as unasserted. Replacing one with a real assertion is how a card actually gets verified; keys are automtg.cards.authoring.verify.EXPECTATION_KEYS.",
